The source is public so you can read it, learn from it and help improve it. It is not open source:
the mod may only be shared through its official releases.

"The Work" = everything in this repository and in this mod's official releases: source code, builds,
voice clips, sounds, pictures and texts, unless a file says it is under another license.
"Official releases" = the author's own Steam Workshop items and GitHub releases.

YOU MAY

1. Read and study the Work.
2. Fork the repository on GitHub, change your fork, and send changes back as pull requests or patches.
3. Build the Work and run your own build on your own computer, for yourself.
4. Download and play the official releases, and show them in videos, streams and screenshots.
5. Link to the official releases anywhere, and add them to Steam Workshop collections.

YOU MAY NOT, without the author's written permission

1. Re-upload or share the Work or a build of it, changed or unchanged, anywhere outside a GitHub fork
   (Steam Workshop, Nexus Mods, other mod sites, Discord, file hosts, modpacks, game copies with the
   mod inside).
2. Use the Work or any part of it (code, voices, sounds, pictures, texts) in another mod, program,
   project or product.
3. Sell the Work or use it commercially.
4. Use the names "R.A.T.S." or the mod's name, the logos or the pictures for anything that is not an
   official release, or in a way that looks official.
5. Remove or change this license or the copyright notices.

